#====================================================================
# DRAFT-kissfft-131-numeric-fftpack-numpy-migration
# 触发事件: kissfft 131 r02 返工（rule4 通过率修正）
#          compfft.py/fastfir.py 依赖 Python2 专有 Numeric/FFTPACK 模块,
#          Python3 环境 ModuleNotFoundError, 以 numpy 语义等价迁移后实跑通过
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-kissfft-131-numeric-fftpack-numpy-migration
trigger_tool:           python3|numpy|Numeric|FFTPACK|popen2|test
phase:                  testing
error_signature:        "No module named 'Numeric'|No module named 'FFT'|ModuleNotFoundError.*Numeric|ModuleNotFoundError.*FFTPACK|from Numeric import|import FFT"

severity:               2
category:               ohos|portability|upstream-test|python3|numpy|legacy-module
match_keywords:         OHOS, Python 2, Python 3, Numeric, FFTPACK, numpy, popen2,
                         test runner, upstream test, module migration, fftnd,
                         real_fft, inverse_fft, ModuleNotFoundError, aarch64

title: 'OHOS upstream Python2 test scripts depending on Numeric/FFTPACK: numpy-equivalent migration'

root_cause: >
  Upstream test scripts written for Python 2 import the Python2-only third-party
  modules Numeric (array/linear algebra) and FFT (FFTPACK wrapper). Python 3
  environments (and pip, which has no distribution for fftpack/numeric) cannot
  provide them, so the scripts fail with ModuleNotFoundError. This is OUTSIDE the
  boundary of existing E269 (port-python-script), whose scope explicitly excludes
  runners depending on Python 2 C extensions or Python2-only third-party packages.

solution: >
  Minimal semantic-equivalent migration to numpy (already available on OHOS as
  numpy 2.5.2 aarch64 wheel):
  1. `from Numeric import *` -> `import numpy as np`;
  2. FFTPACK wrapper calls -> numpy.fft equivalents:
     FFT.fftnd(x)->np.fft.fftn(np.asarray(x,dtype=complex)); inverse_fft(fm)->
     np.fft.ifft(fm); fft(h,nfft)->np.fft.fft(h,nfft); real-optimized baseline
     -> np.fft.fft complex baseline;
  3. Numeric array/reduction funcs -> np.* (array/reshape/size/conjugate/sum/
     convolve/vdot/concatenate);
  4. popen2.Popen3 -> subprocess.Popen(stdin=PIPE, stdout=PIPE); binary IO in
     wb/rb mode; bytes join b''.join for struct.pack output (Python3);
  5. dict.has_key -> `in` (shared with E269 syntax-level fixes).
  Keep test corpus and assertion semantics (SNR thresholds) unchanged; library
  source untouched.

verification_cmd: >
  python3 compfft.py -n 4 -u ./kf_float; python3 compfft.py -n 2,3 -u ./kf_float;
  python3 compfft.py -n 3,4,4 -u ./kf_float; python3 fastfir.py -l 500 -n 128
  (kissfft 131 r02: SNR 143-148dB / snr=135.5, all exit 0; included in
  dual-caliber ledger 17/20 = 85.0%, 17/17 = 100% on current config)

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           numeric-fftpack-numpy-migration
rec_description:        Replace Python2-only Numeric/FFTPACK imports with semantic
                        numpy.fft/np.* equivalents in upstream test scripts; keep
                        assertions; only for pure-numeric module dependencies.
rec_auto_fix:           true
rec_impl:               test-portability-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      document-platform-difference-only
fallback_description:   If migrating scripts is not acceptable, record the
                        Numeric/FFTPACK absence as a platform dependency difference
                        in the ledger without changing the test scripts.
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          ledger-only

forbid_1_pattern:       gtest_filter.*compfft|skip.*fastfir|exclude.*Numeric
forbid_1_reason:        Disabling or skipping the failing tests hides platform
                        portability evidence and is not a fix.
forbid_2_pattern:       snr.*< 10|SNR.*threshold.*100.*removed|pass.*without.*run
forbid_2_reason:        Arbitrarily relaxing SNR thresholds or claiming pass without
                        actually running masks real regressions.

related:                E269
similar_to:             E269
path:                   B (knowledge extension; module-level numpy migration is a
                        new difference beyond E269 syntax-level porting)
dedup:                  doc/ miss; graph/ miss; drafts/ miss (E2164 "Numeric" is an
                        unrelated version-string topic); index.tsv miss; E269 partial
                        (syntax-level only, explicitly excludes Python2-only modules)
affected_scope:         OHOS aarch64 C/C++ libs whose upstream Python2 test scripts
                        depend on Numeric/FFTPACK or similar Python2-only numeric
                        modules
verification_evidence:  compfft.py + fastfir.py migrated and run (SNR 143-148dB /
                        snr=135.5, exit 0); ledger 17/20=85%, 17/17=100%;
                        conan create/verify PASS; W3 local CI green
pr_prefix:              【知识库扩展】
